A||||9||recluse||Just installed bored out TB/intake, Not running right! ||||5||
Z||000000||recluse||12-09-2001||01:06 AM||||I installed the bored out throttle body and intake from Darrell Morse and while I was there an adjustable fuel pressure regulator.  I dont have a fuel pressure gauge yet so I dont know how much pressure im running.  The problem is it misses (spits and sputters) when i accelerate normally at around 3000-4000 RPM. Kinda like it hits a dead spot.  But if I hold the throttle wide open it seems to rev smoothly and normally. If I just cruise along at around 3000 or so it does it, but not so much at high RPMs.  It seems like its not getting enough fuel or maybe too much?  I adjusted it a few times but it seems to be the same.  Is it just a matter of getting it adjusted right or could it be something else?  Its only when I hold the RPMs steady or slowly accelerate.  Thanks<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-09-2001||01:41 AM||||remove the aftermarket fuel pressure regulator, then see what results you will net<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||12-09-2001||03:33 AM||||Hey Recluse!<BR>Have you checked for vacuume leaks?<BR>What other mods do you have on the engine?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||recluse||12-09-2001||12:43 PM||||No vacume leaks that I can find.  The only mods I have are a cold air intake, accel coil, underdrive pully, and low temp fan switch. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||12-09-2001||05:10 PM||||You are asking the forum what the problem could be knowing that it could be the fact that the adj fpr isn't adjusted right?  Seems to me that would be the first place to look.  Get a gauge on there and see what it is reading and get it adjusted properly.  I would set it to around 40 psi or so and go from there.  It could be dumping too much fuel.<P>Do that and if your car still does that then check for vacuum leaks.  If it still does it then come back and ask for some help.  You might not think you have a vacuum leak but just cause you can't hear it doesn't mean it is not there.  Run some smoke through the vacuum lines and see if you see it leaking out anywhere.<P>------------------<BR>Sold Nitrous 85 GT.<BR>Looking for another.<BR>FOR SALE: Aluminum v6 block.<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||5
Z||000005||Raydar||12-09-2001||06:17 PM||||First thing that I would do is go back to the stock coil and see if the miss is still there. I've heard meny stories on this Forum about Accel coils "going south". Even relatively new ones. <BR>You also might have a dead spot on your TPS, but that's a shot in the dark. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||recluse||12-09-2001||06:29 PM||||Fixed it....  It was the regulator.  I made the stock one adjustable by following the instructions on some website and turns out the instructions where wrong causing slight damage to the spring assembly.  Runs good now except for the high idle that I still cant figure out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||jimmybpei||12-09-2001||06:49 PM||||Ok so what do you think of the tb and plenum is it well worth the money or not.<P>Thinking stongly on purchaseing this combo myself. Even though i have heard lots of good stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000008||recluse||12-09-2001||06:57 PM||||I am happy with the set up.  I can tell a differnce, it seems to rev quicker at higher RPMs and has better throttle response. If im cruising along in 5th and drop it down to 3rd to take off it gets up and goes better than before.  I might be able to get even more when I get a pressure gauge and get it adjusted right. BTW Darrell Morse does great machine work.||||reg||1
